// ===========================================================================
// engine/system/null_interrupt.emp — the no-op interrupt handler
// ===========================================================================
// The tolerant IRQ handler: `rte`, does nothing.
//
// CURRENTLY UNREFERENCED (2026-08-04). It used to serve IRQ1/2/3/5/7 (external
// + NMI); review item 27's owner ruling — "a spurious or unexpected interrupt
// must halt loudly in BOTH shapes" — repointed all five at ErrorExcept, so no
// vector cell names this proc today. It is deliberately KEPT, not deleted: it
// is the engine's only tolerant-IRQ primitive, and whether the ROM still needs
// one belongs to the blocked release-shape error-handler strip parcel
// (docs/DEFERRED_WORK.md) — that parcel has to answer "what does release do on
// a fault?" and this is one of the candidate answers for the NON-fault levels.
// Do NOT repoint the vector table back at it without an owner ruling; see the
// policy block at the top of vectors.emp.
//
// It deliberately does NOT live in vectors.emp
// (that file is the fixed org-0 image); it sits near the ROM tail, just before the
// exception-vector stubs (error_handler). Placed at its frozen boundary key by
// the chainer.
// ===========================================================================

module engine.system.null_interrupt in null_interrupt

section null_interrupt (cpu: m68000) {
    pub proc NullInterrupt () clobbers() {
        rte
    }
}
